ckage-less sibling import resolves under the by-path load, so harness.<name> lookups in both unit tests keep working.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_provisioning.py:121 `harness._create_scratch_project(\"RBTEST\")`; :127 `harness._PROJECT_TEMPLATE`; :210-213 `harness._REQUIRED_ISSUE_TYPES`/`_REQUIRED_FIELDS`","conftest.py:26-31 loads the module via importlib spec_from_file_location under name `_live_jira_dc_conftest_under_test`","conftest.py:48-66 shows the file already needs explicit sys.path insertion to import package-less siblings/scripts"],"finding":"The plan's split mechanism does not state how the by-path-loaded module's SURFACE is preserved: both unit tests reference moved helpers as attributes of the loaded conftest module (e.g. harness._create_scratch_project, harness._PROJECT_TEMPLATE, harness._REQUIRED_ISSUE_TYPES/_REQUIRED_FIELDS, harness._assert_project_capabilities). A plain move to a sibling file breaks those attribute lookups unless conftest re-imports the moved names into its own namespace — and because conftest is loaded package-less by path, that re-import needs the same sys.path handling the file already performs. AC#3 states the constraint but the plan never specifies the re-export/import step that satisfies it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f569951c16e17fd1e","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan body 'a split must follow call-graph seams' + AC line 3","norm_id":"n355b432be16ad91f","priority":0.7556,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["After extracting the provisioning cluster to a sibling file, `pytest tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_provisioning.py` fails with AttributeError on harness._create_scratch_project / harness._PROJECT_TEMPLATE"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_